// The calling AI tool may deliver args as {query: '<json string>'} (n8n's
// AI-tool-calling path serializes structured arguments this way) instead of
// named fields directly. Normalize either shape to a plain {draft_id, session_id}.
const raw = $input.first().json || {};
let out = raw;

if (typeof raw.query !== 'undefined') {
  if (typeof raw.query === 'string') {
    const s = raw.query.trim().replace(/^```(?:json)?/i, '').replace(/```$/, '').trim();
    try {
      out = JSON.parse(s);
    } catch (e) {
      // The model sent a bare draft id rather than a JSON object. Accept it.
      out = /^drf_[A-Za-z0-9]+$/.test(s) ? { draft_id: s } : {};
    }
  } else {
    out = raw.query;
  }
}

const draftId = String(out.draft_id || '').trim();
if (!draftId) {
  throw new Error(
    'deploy_draft was called without a draft_id. Pass {"draft_id":"drf_...","session_id":"..."}. ' +
    'Received: ' + JSON.stringify(raw).slice(0, 300)
  );
}

return [{ json: { draft_id: draftId, session_id: out.session_id || null } }];

// Build the Azure resource id and PUT body from the draft.
// Deliberately deterministic: the same draft always yields the same resource
// id, so a redeploy updates in place rather than creating a twin.
const crypto = require('crypto');
const res = $input.first().json || {};
const trigger = $('Normalize Query Input').first().json;

// "Get Draft Artifact" runs with fullResponse+neverError so a 404 surfaces as
// a readable message here instead of flowing on as a body-less "draft".
const httpStatus = Number(res.statusCode) || 0;
if (httpStatus === 0) {
  throw new Error(
    'Could not reach the sentinel-agent sidecar at http://sentinel-agent:8000 to load draft ' +
    (trigger.draft_id || '(unknown)') + '. Check the container is up and on the same compose network.'
  );
}
if (httpStatus === 404) {
  throw new Error('No draft ' + trigger.draft_id + ' exists. Call list_drafts to see valid ids.');
}
if (httpStatus !== 200) {
  const d = typeof res.body === 'object' ? JSON.stringify(res.body) : String(res.body);
  throw new Error('Loading draft ' + trigger.draft_id + ' failed with HTTP ' + httpStatus + '. ' + d.slice(0, 300));
}
const draft = typeof res.body === 'string' ? JSON.parse(res.body) : res.body;

const sub = $env.AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID;
const rg = $env.AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP;
const ws = $env.AZURE_WORKSPACE_NAME;
const location = $env.AZURE_LOCATION || 'eastus';

if (!sub || !rg || !ws) {
  throw new Error('Azure config missing: set AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID, AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP and AZURE_WORKSPACE_NAME in .env, then restart n8n.');
}
if (!draft.artifact) {
  throw new Error('Draft ' + draft.id + ' has no artifact (status: ' + draft.status + '). Nothing to deploy.');
}
if (draft.status !== 'validated') {
  throw new Error('Draft ' + draft.id + " is '" + draft.status + "'. Only a validated draft can be deployed.");
}

const DEPLOYABLE_KINDS = ['parser', 'analytic_rule', 'workbook'];
if (!DEPLOYABLE_KINDS.includes(draft.kind)) {
  throw new Error('Draft ' + draft.id + " is a '" + draft.kind + "' — that's a document, not a resource that deploys to Azure. Hand it to the analyst directly instead.");
}

const workspaceResourceId = '/subscriptions/' + sub + '/resourceGroups/' + rg + '/providers/Microsoft.OperationalInsights/workspaces/' + ws;

// uuid5-equivalent: sha1 over a fixed namespace + name with the version and
// variant bits set. Stable GUID for a workbook, no uuid library needed.
function stableGuid(name) {
  const NS = '6f9619ff8b86d011b42d00c04fc964ff';
  // uuid5 hashes the namespace as raw bytes followed by the name's UTF-8 bytes.
  // Feed the hash a latin1 string of those same bytes so no Buffer global is
  // needed — n8n's task-runner sandbox does not reliably provide one.
  let nsBytes = '';
  for (let i = 0; i < NS.length; i += 2) {
    nsBytes += String.fromCharCode(parseInt(NS.substr(i, 2), 16));
  }
  const nameBytes = unescape(encodeURIComponent(name));
  const hex = crypto.createHash('sha1').update(nsBytes + nameBytes, 'latin1').digest('hex');
  const bytes = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < 32; i += 2) bytes.push(parseInt(hex.substr(i, 2), 16));
  bytes[6] = (bytes[6] & 0x0f) | 0x50;
  bytes[8] = (bytes[8] & 0x3f) | 0x80;
  const h = bytes.map(function (x) { return x.toString(16).padStart(2, '0'); }).join('');
  return h.slice(0, 8) + '-' + h.slice(8, 12) + '-' + h.slice(12, 16) + '-' + h.slice(16, 20) + '-' + h.slice(20);
}

let out;
if (draft.kind === 'parser') {
  const yaml = draft.artifact;
  const pick = function (key) {
    const m = yaml.match(new RegExp('^' + key + ':\\s*(.+)$', 'm'));
    return m ? m[1].trim().replace(/^['\"]|['\"]$/g, '') : '';
  };
  const alias = pick('FunctionAlias') || draft.name;
  const titleMatch = yaml.match(/^\s*Title:\s*(.+)$/m);
  const displayName = titleMatch ? titleMatch[1].trim().replace(/^['\"]|['\"]$/g, '') : alias;

  // FunctionQuery is a YAML block scalar: everything indented beneath it.
  const qStart = yaml.indexOf('FunctionQuery:');
  if (qStart === -1) throw new Error('parser YAML has no FunctionQuery');
  const lines = yaml.slice(qStart).split('\n').slice(1);
  const body = [];
  for (const line of lines) {
    if (line.trim() === '') { body.push(''); continue; }
    if (!/^\s/.test(line)) break;
    body.push(line.replace(/^ {4}/, ''));
  }
  const query = body.join('\n').replace(/\s+$/, '');
  if (!query) throw new Error('could not extract FunctionQuery from the parser YAML');

  const properties = {
    category: pick('Category') || 'Microsoft Sentinel Parser',
    displayName: displayName,
    functionAlias: alias,
    query: query,
    version: 2
  };
  out = {
    resource_type: 'savedSearch',
    resource_id: workspaceResourceId + '/savedSearches/' + alias,
    api_version: '2020-08-01',
    name: alias,
    request_body: { properties: properties }
  };
} else if (draft.kind === 'analytic_rule') {
  const yaml = draft.artifact;
  const pick = function (key) {
    const m = yaml.match(new RegExp('^' + key + ':\\s*(.+)$', 'm'));
    return m ? m[1].trim().replace(/^['"]|['"]$/g, '') : '';
  };
  const pickBlock = function (key) {
    const start = yaml.indexOf(key + ':');
    if (start === -1) return '';
    const lines = yaml.slice(start).split('\n').slice(1);
    const body = [];
    for (const line of lines) {
      if (line.trim() === '') { body.push(''); continue; }
      if (!/^\s/.test(line)) break;
      body.push(line.replace(/^ {2}/, ''));
    }
    return body.join('\n').replace(/\s+$/, '');
  };
  const pickFlowArray = function (key) {
    const m = yaml.match(new RegExp('^' + key + ':\\s*\\[([^\\]]*)\\]', 'm'));
    if (!m) return [];
    return m[1].split(',').map(function (s) { return s.trim().replace(/^['"]|['"]$/g, ''); }).filter(Boolean);
  };
  const toIso8601 = function (short) {
    const m = String(short || '').trim().match(/^(\d+)\s*([mhd])$/i);
    if (!m) throw new Error("cannot convert duration '" + short + "' to ISO-8601 (expected e.g. 5m, 1h, 1d)");
    const n = m[1];
    const unit = m[2].toLowerCase();
    if (unit === 'm') return 'PT' + n + 'M';
    if (unit === 'h') return 'PT' + n + 'H';
    return 'P' + n + 'D';
  };
  const OPERATORS = { gt: 'GreaterThan', lt: 'LessThan', eq: 'Equal', ne: 'NotEqual' };

  const ruleId = pick('id');
  if (!ruleId) throw new Error('analytic rule YAML has no id');
  const query = pickBlock('query');
  if (!query) throw new Error('could not extract query from the analytic rule YAML');
  const description = pickBlock('description') || pick('description');

  const connectorsBlock = pickBlock('requiredDataConnectors');
  const requiredDataConnectors = connectorsBlock.split(/\n(?=\s*-\s*connectorId:)/).filter(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).map(function (chunk) {
    const idMatch = chunk.match(/connectorId:\s*(.+)/);
    const typesMatch = chunk.match(/dataTypes:\s*\[([^\]]*)\]/);
    return {
      connectorId: idMatch ? idMatch[1].trim().replace(/^['"]|['"]$/g, '') : '',
      dataTypes: typesMatch ? typesMatch[1].split(',').map(function (s) { return s.trim().replace(/^['"]|['"]$/g, ''); }).filter(Boolean) : []
    };
  });

  const entitiesBlock = pickBlock('entityMappings');
  const entityMappings = entitiesBlock.split(/\n(?=\s*-\s*entityType:)/).filter(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).map(function (chunk) {
    const typeMatch = chunk.match(/entityType:\s*(\S+)/);
    const fieldMappings = [];
    const fmRe = /\{\s*identifier:\s*([^,}]+?)\s*,\s*columnName:\s*([^}]+?)\s*\}/g;
    let fm;
    while ((fm = fmRe.exec(chunk)) !== null) {
      fieldMappings.push({ identifier: fm[1].trim(), columnName: fm[2].trim() });
    }
    return { entityType: typeMatch ? typeMatch[1].trim() : '', fieldMappings: fieldMappings };
  });

  const properties = {
    displayName: pick('name') || draft.name,
    description: description,
    severity: pick('severity') || 'Medium',
    enabled: true,
    query: query,
    queryFrequency: toIso8601(pick('queryFrequency')),
    queryPeriod: toIso8601(pick('queryPeriod')),
    triggerOperator: OPERATORS[pick('triggerOperator') || 'gt'] || 'GreaterThan',
    triggerThreshold: parseInt(pick('triggerThreshold') || '0', 10),
    tactics: pickFlowArray('tactics'),
    techniques: pickFlowArray('techniques'),
    requiredDataConnectors: requiredDataConnectors,
    entityMappings: entityMappings,
    incidentConfiguration: { createIncident: true, groupingConfiguration: { enabled: false } }
  };
  out = {
    resource_type: 'alertRule',
    resource_id: workspaceResourceId + '/providers/Microsoft.SecurityInsights/alertRules/' + ruleId,
    api_version: '2023-11-01',
    name: ruleId,
    request_body: { kind: 'Scheduled', properties: properties }
  };
} else {
  const guid = stableGuid(draft.name);
  const properties = {
    displayName: draft.name,
    category: 'sentinel',
    serializedData: draft.artifact,
    sourceId: workspaceResourceId,
    version: 'Notebook/1.0'
  };
  out = {
    resource_type: 'workbook',
    resource_id: '/subscriptions/' + sub + '/resourceGroups/' + rg + '/providers/Microsoft.Insights/workbooks/' + guid,
    api_version: '2023-06-01',
    name: guid,
    request_body: { location: location, kind: 'shared', properties: properties }
  };
}

out.draft_id = draft.id;
out.draft_kind = draft.kind;
out.draft_name = draft.name;
out.session_id = trigger.session_id || null;
out.get_url = 'https://management.azure.com' + out.resource_id + '?api-version=' + out.api_version;
return [{ json: out }];

// GET-before-PUT tells us create vs update, and catches the common
// auth/role misconfigurations before a PUT ever fires.
const res = $input.first().json || {};
const plan = $('Build Azure Request').first().json;

// A transport-level failure (no TCP/TLS/DNS, or a credential n8n could not
// resolve) never produces a statusCode. Those arrive here as HTTP 0 with an
// undefined body, which is the least actionable error the workflow can emit —
// so name the actual causes instead of printing "HTTP 0. undefined".
const status = Number(res.statusCode) || 0;

if (status === 0) {
  const netErr = res.error || res.message || (res.body && res.body.message) || '';
  throw new Error(
    'GET before deploy never reached Azure (no HTTP response). ' +
    'This is a transport/credential problem, not an Azure rejection. Check, in order:\n' +
    '  1. The OAuth2 credential "Azure Management (client credentials)" exists in n8n and is ' +
    'attached to BOTH the "GET Current Resource" and "PUT to Azure" nodes. A missing or ' +
    'unresolvable credential fails before any request is sent.\n' +
    '  2. Grant Type = Client Credentials, Access Token URL = ' +
    'https://login.microsoftonline.com/<AZURE_TENANT_ID>/oauth2/v2.0/token, ' +
    'Scope = https://management.azure.com/.default, Authentication = "Body".\n' +
    '  3. The n8n container can reach login.microsoftonline.com and management.azure.com ' +
    '(egress proxy / firewall / DNS).\n' +
    '  URL attempted: ' + (plan.get_url || '(none)') +
    (netErr ? '\n  Underlying error: ' + String(netErr).slice(0, 300) : '')
  );
}

const action = status === 200 ? 'update' : 'create';

if (status !== 200 && status !== 404) {
  const detail = typeof res.body === 'object'
    ? JSON.stringify(res.body).slice(0, 400)
    : String(res.body === undefined ? '(no body)' : res.body).slice(0, 400);
  let hint = '';
  if (status === 401) hint = ' — token rejected. Check the OAuth2 credential scope is https://management.azure.com/.default';
  if (status === 403) hint = ' — the service principal lacks a role here. Parsers need Log Analytics Contributor; workbooks need Monitoring Contributor; analytic rules need Sentinel Contributor.';
  throw new Error('GET before deploy failed with HTTP ' + status + hint + '. ' + detail);
}

plan.action = action;
plan.put_url = 'https://management.azure.com' + plan.resource_id + '?api-version=' + plan.api_version;
return [{ json: plan }];

// PUT is idempotent by resource name, which is what makes the retry above
// safe: a timed-out request can be replayed without risking a duplicate.
const res = $input.first().json;
const plan = $('Decide Action').first().json;
const status = res.statusCode || 0;
const ok = status === 200 || status === 201;

let error = null;
let outcome = ok ? 'deployed' : 'failed';

if (!ok) {
  const body = typeof res.body === 'object' ? JSON.stringify(res.body) : String(res.body || '');
  if (status === 409) {
    error = 'HTTP 409 Conflict — the resource changed since it was read here. Run deploy_draft again to pick up the latest state before overwriting. ' + body.slice(0, 300);
  } else if (status === 403) {
    error = 'HTTP 403 Forbidden — the service principal lacks a role assignment. Parsers need Log Analytics Contributor; workbooks need Monitoring Contributor; analytic rules need Sentinel Contributor on the resource group. ' + body.slice(0, 300);
  } else if (status === 401) {
    error = 'HTTP 401 — token rejected. Check the OAuth2 credential uses scope https://management.azure.com/.default. ' + body.slice(0, 300);
  } else if (status === 400) {
    error = 'HTTP 400 — malformed request body. This is a bug in the deploy workflow, not the model. ' + body.slice(0, 400);
  } else if (status === 0) {
    outcome = 'unknown';
    error = 'No response after retries. The PUT is idempotent so this may still have applied — GET the resource to confirm before retrying.';
  } else {
    error = 'HTTP ' + status + ': ' + body.slice(0, 400);
  }
}

return [{ json: {
  draft_id: plan.draft_id,
  resource_type: plan.resource_type,
  resource_id: plan.resource_id,
  action: plan.action,
  status: outcome,
  http_status: status,
  request_body: plan.request_body,
  response_body: ok ? (res.body || null) : null,
  error: error,
  session_id: plan.session_id
} }];

const r = $('Classify Result').first().json;
const rec = $input.first().json;
const verb = r.action === 'create' ? 'Created' : 'Updated';
return [{ json: {
  deployment_id: rec.deployment_id,
  draft_id: r.draft_id,
  status: r.status,
  message: r.status === 'deployed'
    ? verb + ' ' + r.resource_type + " '" + r.resource_id.split('/').pop() + "' successfully."
    : (r.status === 'unknown'
        ? 'Deployment state is UNKNOWN — ' + r.error
        : 'Deployment failed — ' + r.error)
} }];
